## Testing policy

<<#IF_TDD_NONE>>
Tests not required for this project.
<</#IF_TDD_NONE>>
<<#IF_TDD_BASIC>>
Write test stubs alongside new code. Every new function needs at least one happy-path test before marking done.
<</#IF_TDD_BASIC>>
<<#IF_TDD_FULL>>
**Full TDD enforced.** Failing test first (RED) → minimal implementation (GREEN) → refactor. Coverage ≥ 80%. Never skip RED.
<</#IF_TDD_FULL>>

## Security non-negotiables

- NEVER hardcode secrets, API keys, or tokens. Use `.env` + `process.env`.
- NEVER commit `.env`. Commit `.env.example` only.
- Validate all user input at system boundaries.
- Parameterised queries only — no string-concatenated SQL.
- If a secret lands in source, stop and flag it immediately.

